---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Software Development Services — Interlaced Pixel" description="Custom application development, systems and networking software, developer tools, and technical discovery from Interlaced Pixel.">
	<header class="page-hero service-page-hero">
		<div class="container narrow reveal">
			<p class="kicker"><span></span> Software development services</p>
			<h1>Bring the hard<br><em>software problem.</em></h1>
			<p>We work with teams to design and build focused software, from a first technical direction to a complete, usable product.</p>
			<div class="button-row">
				<a href="/contact" class="button primary">Discuss your project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
				<a href="/projects" class="button secondary">See selected work</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="section service-detail-section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading reveal">
				<div><p class="kicker">How we can help</p><h2>From product ideas<br>to deep technical work.</h2></div>
				<p class="section-intro">Engagements are shaped around the problem, the people using the software, and the constraints the solution has to meet.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="service-detail-list">
				<article class="service-detail reveal" id="application-development">
					<span class="service-index">01 / APPLICATIONS</span>
					<div><h3>Application development</h3><p>Build new software around the people who need it: desktop applications, product features, and interfaces that make a workflow simpler.</p><ul><li>Product and feature implementation</li><li>Interface and application architecture</li><li>Integration with existing services and systems</li></ul></div>
				</article>
				<article class="service-detail reveal" id="systems-software">
					<span class="service-index">02 / SYSTEMS</span>
					<div><h3>Systems & networking</h3><p>Develop the software beneath the interface, where efficiency, portability, and predictable behavior are part of the product.</p><ul><li>Networking software and protocols</li><li>Performance-sensitive C and C++ development</li><li>Cross-platform utilities and infrastructure</li></ul></div>
				</article>
				<article class="service-detail reveal" id="developer-tools">
					<span class="service-index">03 / DEVELOPER EXPERIENCE</span>
					<div><h3>Developer tools</h3><p>Make engineering workflows more useful with focused tools that surface information clearly and fit into the tools teams already use.</p><ul><li>Editor extensions and workflow utilities</li><li>Internal tools for technical teams</li><li>Build, test, and diagnostic workflow improvements</li></ul></div>
				</article>
				<article class="service-detail reveal" id="technical-discovery">
					<span class="service-index">04 / DISCOVERY</span>
					<div><h3>Technical discovery & prototypes</h3><p>Reduce uncertainty before committing to a larger build. We can help clarify requirements, compare approaches, and test the riskiest assumption with a focused prototype.</p><ul><li>Problem and constraint mapping</li><li>Architecture and implementation planning</li><li>Working prototypes to validate direction</li></ul></div>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-contrast service-fit-section">
		<div class="container approach-grid">
			<div class="approach-intro reveal">
				<p class="kicker light">A good fit</p>
				<h2>Technical challenges deserve clear thinking.</h2>
				<p>We’re a small independent studio suited to focused work that benefits from direct collaboration and careful engineering.</p>
			</div>
			<ul class="fit-list">
				<li><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><p>You have a real user or workflow problem to solve.</p></li>
				<li><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><p>The solution has meaningful technical constraints.</p></li>
				<li><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><p>You value clear communication and a maintainable result.</p></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="container reveal">
			<p class="kicker">The first step is a conversation</p>
			<h2>Tell us what you’re trying to solve.</h2>
			<a href="/contact" class="button light-button">Discuss a project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
